-- California: Business and Professions Code, Division 8, Chapter 25 (the California AI
-- Transparency Act), as amended by SB 1000 (approved 30 September 2026, an urgency
-- statute in effect on approval). Sections 22757.1 (the definitions used here),
-- 22757.3(a), 22757.3.1, 22757.5 and 22757.6.
--
-- Sources: source/ca-sb1000-2026-enrolled.html for 22757.1, 22757.3 and 22757.5 as
-- amended; source/ca-ab853-2025-chaptered.html for 22757.3.1 and 22757.6, which SB 1000
-- does not amend. Quotations are copied from source/text/.
--
-- ONE VINTAGE ONLY. Sections 22757.1, 22757.3 and 22757.5 read differently from
-- 2 August 2026 (when the chapter became operative) to 29 September 2026: that text,
-- SB 942 as amended by AB 853, had a 1,000,000-user threshold and a manifest-disclosure
-- option. It is not encoded, and a question dated in that window refuses.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`

§ `The judgements 22757.3(a) hands to someone, and one fact this chapter alone needs`

DECLARE `California 22757.3 inputs` HAS
    -- 22757.3(a): "To the extent it is technically feasible"
    `including a latent disclosure is technically feasible`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- 22757.3(a)(2): "The disclosure is permanent or extraordinarily difficult to remove or tamper with."
    `the disclosure is permanent or extraordinarily difficult to remove or tamper with` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- 22757.3(a)(3): a fact about the provider's own tool
    `the disclosure is compatible with the covered provider's disclosure verification tool` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `22757.6 and SB 1000 -- which text applies on a date`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.6 (AB 853); SB 1000 (2026), s.8
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text of this chapter in force from 2 August to 29 September 2026 (SB 942 as amended by AB 853) is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of this chapter in force from 2 August to 29 September 2026 (SB 942 as amended by AB 853) is not encoded"

-- 22757.6: "This chapter shall become operative on August 2, 2026."
-- SB 1000, s.8: an urgency statute that "shall go into immediate effect"; approved by
-- the Governor on 30 September 2026.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SB 1000 text of this chapter governs on` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF d AT LEAST (YMD 2026 9 30) THEN TRUE
           IF d AT LEAST (YMD 2026 8 2)  THEN `the text of this chapter in force from 2 August to 29 September 2026 (SB 942 as amended by AB 853) is not encoded`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `22757.1 -- definitions`

-- (e): "'Covered provider' means a person that creates, codes, or otherwise produces a
-- generative artificial intelligence system that is publicly accessible within the
-- geographic boundaries of the state." No user threshold since SB 1000.
-- "a person": nothing in the sources encoded here defines "person", so whether a state,
-- local, or tribal government is one is not answered. NOTES fork F15, raised by the
-- independent test pass (W-04 to W-06).
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.1(e), as amended by SB 1000
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`whether a state, local, or tribal government is a "person" under 22757.1(e) is not answered by the sources encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether a state, local, or tribal government is a \"person\" under 22757.1(e) is not answered by the sources encoded"

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.1(e), as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provider is a covered provider in California` provider MEANS
    IF   provider's `it is a state, local, or tribal government`
    THEN `whether a state, local, or tribal government is a "person" under 22757.1(e) is not answered by the sources encoded`
    ELSE provider's `its system is publicly accessible within California`

-- (l): "'Minor modification' means any of the following alterations:
--   (1) A change to brightness, contrast, or color. (2) Sharpening. (3) Saturating.
--   (4) File resizing. (5) Scaling. (6) Cropping. (7) File format conversions.
--   (8) Denoising and removal of background noise in audio."
-- "means any of the following" makes this list CLOSED. "Applying filters" and
-- "resampling", on Washington's list, are not on it; nor is compression or the
-- removal of red-eye. Contrast Washington s.2(4), which is open.
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.1(l), as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN a IS A `kind of alteration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a minor modification in California` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a change to brightness, contrast, or color` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sharpening`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `saturating`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `resizing`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `scaling`                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cropping`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `file format conversion`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `denoising`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal of background noise in audio`       THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is image, video, or audio content` content IF
        elem `image` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `video` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `audio` (content's `the kinds it contains`)

-- 22757.3(a): content "created or altered, except by minor modification, by the
-- covered provider's GenAI system".
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the GenAI system created or altered it, except by minor modification` content IF
        content's `how it came to exist` EQUALS `generated by an AI system`
    OR  any (GIVEN a YIELD NOT `it is a minor modification in California` a)
            (content's `the alterations an AI system made to it`)

§ `22757.5 -- what the chapter does not reach`

-- "(a) This chapter does not apply to any product, service, internet website, or
-- application that provides exclusively non-user-generated videogames.
-- (b) Before January 1, 2029, this chapter does not apply to a GenAI system that is
-- designed to primarily function as assistive technology."
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.5, as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `22757.5 takes the provider's system outside the chapter on` provider d IF
        provider's `its product exclusively provides non-user-generated videogames`
    OR  (    provider's `its system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology`
         AND d LESS THAN (YMD 2029 1 1))

§ `22757.3(a) -- the latent disclosure`

-- "To the extent it is technically feasible, a covered provider shall include a latent
-- disclosure that meets all of the following criteria in any image, video, or audio
-- content, or content that is any combination thereof, created or altered, except by
-- minor modification, by the covered provider's GenAI system".
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.3(a), 22757.5, 22757.6, as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, inputs IS A `California 22757.3 inputs`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`22757.3(a) requires the provider to include a latent disclosure` content provider inputs d MEANS
    IF `the SB 1000 text of this chapter governs on` d
    THEN    `the provider is a covered provider in California` provider
        AND NOT `22757.5 takes the provider's system outside the chapter on` provider d
        AND `it is image, video, or audio content` content
        AND `the GenAI system created or altered it, except by minor modification` content
        AND inputs's `including a latent disclosure is technically feasible`
    ELSE FALSE

-- (a)(1): "The disclosure conveys all of the following information, either directly or
-- through a link to a permanent internet website:
--   (A) The name of the covered provider.
--   (B) The name and version information of the GenAI system that created or altered
--       the content.
--   (C) The time and date of the content's creation or alteration.
--   (D) A unique identifier.
--   (E) Whether the GenAI system created or altered the content.
--   (F) On and after January 1, 2029, whether the GenAI system is designed to primarily
--       function as assistive technology."
DECLARE `item a latent disclosure must convey` IS ONE OF
    `(A) the name of the covered provider`
    `(B) the name and version information of the GenAI system`
    `(C) the time and date of the content's creation or alteration`
    `(D) a unique identifier`
    `(E) whether the GenAI system created or altered the content`

GIVEN m IS A `C2PA manifest`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, i IS AN `item a latent disclosure must convey`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manifest conveys` m provider i IF
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `(A) the name of the covered provider` THEN
            m's `the signer it names`    EQUALS provider's `its name`
        OR  m's `the generator it names` EQUALS provider's `its name`
    WHEN `(B) the name and version information of the GenAI system` THEN
            NOT m's `the generator it names` EQUALS ""
        AND NOT m's `the generator version it names` EQUALS ""
    WHEN `(C) the time and date of the content's creation or alteration` THEN
        NOT m's `the time it records` EQUALS ""
    WHEN `(D) a unique identifier` THEN
        NOT m's `the identifier it carries` EQUALS ""
    WHEN `(E) whether the GenAI system created or altered the content` THEN
            elem `trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
        OR  elem `composite with trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
        OR  m's `it carries an AI disclosure assertion`

@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.3(a)(1)(F), as amended by SB 1000
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`whether a manifest conveys item (F) is not modelled` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether a manifest conveys item (F), whether the GenAI system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology, is not modelled"

-- Which of (A)-(E) the content's latent disclosure does NOT convey. No manifest:
-- all five are missing.
-- In the 2 August - 29 September 2026 window the list itself was different (SB 1000
-- added (E)), so the question refuses there rather than answer with SB 1000's list.
-- Before 2 August 2026 no list was law; the answer then describes what is carried
-- against SB 1000's list, and no duty attaches to it. Item (F), from 2029, is not
-- asked here; `the content's latent disclosure meets 22757.3(a)` refuses for it.
-- Raised by the independent test pass (ED-2, ED-5, ED-6, C-15, P-17, X-04; C-03, C-17).
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.3(a)(1), as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `item a latent disclosure must convey`
`the items in 22757.3(a)(1) the disclosure does not convey` content provider d MEANS
    IF d AT LEAST (YMD 2026 8 2) AND d LESS THAN (YMD 2026 9 30)
    THEN REFUSE "the text of this chapter in force from 2 August to 29 September 2026 (SB 942 as amended by AB 853) is not encoded"
    ELSE CONSIDER content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the five items`
         WHEN JUST m  THEN filter (GIVEN i YIELD NOT `the manifest conveys` m provider i) `the five items`
    WHERE
        `the five items` MEANS LIST `(A) the name of the covered provider`,
                                    `(B) the name and version information of the GenAI system`,
                                    `(C) the time and date of the content's creation or alteration`,
                                    `(D) a unique identifier`,
                                    `(E) whether the GenAI system created or altered the content`

-- (a)(1)-(4) together. (4): "The disclosure is compliant or interoperable with widely
-- recognized industry standards." A C2PA manifest is taken to be. NOTES fork F6.
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.3(a)(1)-(4), as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, inputs IS A `California 22757.3 inputs`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the content's latent disclosure meets 22757.3(a)` content provider inputs d MEANS
    IF d AT LEAST (YMD 2029 1 1)
    THEN `whether a manifest conveys item (F) is not modelled`
    ELSE     null (`the items in 22757.3(a)(1) the disclosure does not convey` content provider d)
         AND inputs's `the disclosure is permanent or extraordinarily difficult to remove or tamper with`
         AND inputs's `the disclosure is compatible with the covered provider's disclosure verification tool`
         AND isJust (content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`)

§ `22757.3.1 -- large online platforms`

-- 22757.1(i): "(1) 'Large online platform' means a public-facing social media platform,
-- file-sharing platform, mass messaging platform, or stand-alone search engine that
-- distributes content to users who did not create or collaborate in creating the
-- content that exceeded 2,000,000 unique monthly users during the preceding 12 months.
-- (2) 'Large online platform' does not include either of the following: (A) A broadband
-- internet access service ... (B) A telecommunications service ..."
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.1(i), as amended by SB 1000
GIVEN platform IS A `the distributing platform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a large online platform` platform IF
        platform's `it is a public-facing social media platform, file-sharing platform, mass messaging platform, or stand-alone search engine`
    AND platform's `it distributes content to users who did not create or collaborate in creating the content`
    AND platform's `its unique monthly users during the preceding 12 months` GREATER THAN 2000000
    AND NOT platform's `it is a broadband internet access service`
    AND NOT platform's `it is a telecommunications service`

DECLARE `what 22757.3.1 requires the interface to make available` IS ONE OF
    `nothing under 22757.3.1`
    `the interface must make available` HAS
        `(i) whether provenance data is available`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
        `(ii) the name of the GenAI system or capture device that created or substantially altered the content` IS A MAYBE STRING
        `(iii) whether any digital signatures are available`                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- 22757.3.1(a)(2)(B): "The user interface required by this paragraph shall make clearly
-- and conspicuously available to users information sufficient to identify the
-- content's authenticity, origin, or history of modification, including, but not
-- limited to, all of the following: (i) Whether provenance data is available. (ii) The
-- name of the GenAI system or capture device that created or substantially altered
-- the content, if applicable. (iii) Whether any digital signatures are available."
-- (c): "This section shall become operative on January 1, 2027."
-- Provenance data "compliant with widely adopted specifications adopted by an
-- established standards-setting body" (a)(1) is read as a C2PA manifest. (ii) is read
-- off the manifest's named generator where it declares a capture or a generative
-- source type; NOTES fork F7 on "substantially altered".
@ref Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.3.1 (AB 853), 22757.1(i)
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, platform IS A `the distributing platform`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `what 22757.3.1 requires the interface to make available`
`what the large online platform's interface must make available` content platform d MEANS
    IF d AT LEAST (YMD 2027 1 1) AND `it is a large online platform` platform
    THEN CONSIDER content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the interface must make available` FALSE NOTHING FALSE
         WHEN JUST m  THEN `the interface must make available`
                              TRUE
                              (IF    elem `digital capture` (m's `the source types it declares`)
                                  OR elem `trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
                                  OR elem `composite with trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
                               THEN JUST (m's `the generator it names`)
                               ELSE NOTHING)
                              TRUE
    ELSE `nothing under 22757.3.1`
